Release signing public key — build-time staging.

Before building an ISO, place the Aether release public key PEM here as:

    aether-release.pub.pem

live-build copies everything in this includes.chroot tree into the image, so
the file lands at /usr/share/aether/updates/aether-release.pub.pem — the exact
path the updater verifier reads (DEFAULT_PUBLIC_KEY in aether-updater.py) and
the path Aether Doctor checks.

Generate the keypair offline with scripts/signing/README.md. Only the PUBLIC
key belongs here. The private key must never be placed in this repository or
any ISO. Sign release manifests with scripts/signing/sign-iso.sh so the matching
<manifest>.sig is produced.

If this file is absent at build time, signed updates report signature MISSING
and the updater refuses to apply upgrades. That is the correct fail-closed
state until a release key is supplied.
